    "show_share": true,
    "description": "As much as 70 percent of the rare diseases in the world are due to genetic abnormalities, often leading to chronic disabilities later in life. Pakistan suffers from a high burden of such disorders due to prevalent practice of inter caste marriages, lack of awareness among people and non-availability of clinical metabolic services, said speakers at the launch of Ek-Sath, an initiative to bridge the disconnect between the public and health educationists about inherited metabolic disorders (IMDs).",
